explanation.text:
The failed run repeatedly sampled a memory-heavy model that saved the 200×200 covariance and Cholesky matrices as transformed parameters, and the process was killed after reaching 100% before any CSV files were written [T0B30:<RANGE>transformed parameters {
  vector[N] mu = H * beta;
  matrix[N, N] K = cov_ard_sqexp(X, rho, alpha, jitter)
                   + diag_matrix(rep_vector(square(sigma), N));
  matrix[N, N] L_K = cholesky_decompose(K);
}</RANGE>] [T0B78:<RANGE>Sampling: 100% (8000/8000)
Killed</RANGE>]. It also initially used unsupported sampler argument names, then removed the R control settings rather than mapping them to PyStan’s accepted names [T0B30:<RANGE>ValueError: {'json': {'adapt_kappa': ['Unknown field.'], 'adapt_gamma': ['Unknown field.'], 'adapt_term_buffer': ['Unknown field.'], 'adapt_delta': ['Unknown fi
eld.'], 'adapt_t0': ['Unknown field.'], 'adapt_init_buffer': ['Unknown field.'], 'max_treedepth': ['Unknown field.'], 'adapt_window': ['Unknown field.']}}</RANGE>] [T0B48:<RANGE>fit = posterior.sample(
        num_chains=4,
        num_warmup=1000,
        num_samples=1000,
        num_thin=2,
        save_warmup=False,
        refresh=200,
    )</RANGE>]. Repeated full 8,000-transition reruns, queued commands, and waits consumed the wall-clock budget, ending in an AgentTimeoutError [R0M.exception]. By contrast, the successful run identified the valid names such as `delta`, `max_depth`, and `init_buffer` [T1B68:<RANGE>max_depth = fields.Integer(validate=validate.Range(min=0))
    delta = fields.Number()
    gamma = fields.Number()
    kappa = fields.Number()
    t0 = fields.Number()
    init_buffer = fields.Integer(validate=validate.Range(min=0))</RANGE>], moved large matrices into local model scope to avoid retaining them in every draw [T1B95:<RANGE>model {
  matrix[N, N] K = cov_ard_sqexp(X, rho, alpha, jitter)
                   + diag_matrix(rep_vector(square(sigma), N));
  matrix[N, N] L_K = cholesky_decompose(K);</RANGE>], and verified all four output files with three rows each for `rho` and `beta` [T1B122].

